{
  "source": "Saved/VFX/SlashArcs_v5_ue.fbx",
  "coord_system": "UE mesh-local centimetres; Blender (x, y, z) -> (x, -y, z).",
  "rim_rule": "outer (gold) rim = the smallest-UV-V vertex of each UV U column; U 0 = swing start (tail, s = 0), U 1 = end (head, s = 1).",
  "normal_note": "normal is a unit vector along the arc plane's normal; it is e1 x e2 of the blade's authored arc plane (generate_slash_arcs_v5.py: horizontal arcs (1,0,0) x (0,cos tilt,sin tilt), vertical arcs (cos yaw,sin yaw,0) x (0,0,1)). s 0 -> 1 runs counter-clockwise about it when sweep_deg > 0 and clockwise when < 0 (winding_about_normal). An arc wound the other way is the same curve, so the sign only matters to whatever drives the ring from an angle: the rim point at parameter s sits at ring angle -s * sweep_deg (Niagara's clockwise-positive ring angle, i.e. -atan2(p.Y, p.X) in mesh-local XY of the ring frame) for every blade.",
  "axes_note": "ring_quat_xyzw is a UE FQuat, x, y, z, w order (pass it straight to UnrealQuat.Rotation(); mathutils: Quaternion((w, x, y, z))). It maps the Niagara ring local frame X=start_dir, Y=Z x X=normal x start_dir, Z=normal into mesh-local space (right-handed). Ring angle of a rim point p = atan2(p.Y, p.X) in that local frame, so a Niagara angular sweep of -sweep_deg covers s 0 -> 1 at constant speed. Niagara ring angle is positive clockwise (particles spawn at angle 0 = local +X = start_dir).",
  "fit_note": "fit_rms_cm = radial RMS of the rim's 24 sample points to the reported circle (centre_cm / radius_cm exactly as written); rim_offplane_rms_cm = their RMS distance along the normal from the circle's plane (0 here: the centre is placed at the rim's mean height along the normal, so the written circle sits on the rim). The arc plane is the one the blade was authored in (generate_slash_arcs_v5.py); the rim is tilted ~10 cm off it per 100 cm of blade width by the blade's cone tilt, which costs the near-full sweeps a few cm of radial stretch (see fit_rms_cm per blade).",
  "samples_note": "samples are at s = i/23 along the rim (U from 0 to 1), pos_cm is the rim point (the gold edge), tangent the swing direction, outward the radial (away from the centre) direction. inner_radius_cm = mean distance of the blade's inner (UV V = 1) edge to the circle centre: the fog band lies between inner_radius_cm and radius_cm.",
